# F7: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material inside (a standing boss), flat top cap F9, clean base at z=10.0; top edge beveled 1.0 deep at 90.0deg included (F8) -- proposed as chamfer_depth (CHECKLIST row 2.4)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F7_Boss, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# the tool rides outside at R + r_tool (convex flank; finish_cylinder's mirror)
# the top edge's 1.0mm bevel is the boss's chamfer_depth, at the included angle the
# model measures; a print that says otherwise is typed here (the three chamfer words are
# pick-two) -- break it with: run Form(tool=<ChamferMill>, surface=F7_Boss)
feature F7_Boss CylinderBoss(dia=16.0, extent=8.0, x=20.0, y=20.0, z=10.0, chamfer_depth=1.0, chamfer_angle=90.0)

# F9: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F9_Top Plane(z=18.0)
